= II/ OBJECTIVES

The objectives of this internship were to fabricate and characterize bio-inspired PDA volatile memristors for neuromorphic applications. Four complementary goals were pursued:
(1) electrochemical investigation of the pH-dependent charge-permselectivity of PDA films and optimization of the proton-doped state via CA treatment;
(2) structural and chemical characterization of the PDA films using XPS, Raman, and AFM to correlate the proton-doped state with the polymer backbone configuration;
(3) fabrication of a Cu/C/PDA/ITO crossbar array incorporating a carbon diffusion barrier to control metal ion injection;
(4) electrical characterization of the DC switching uniformity, pulsed endurance up to $10^6$ cycles, and STP dynamics to evaluate device reliability for neuromorphic computing.
